    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1194">

                <pb facs="0975" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5317.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-22T15:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 21, 11 p.m. The most stringent orders were given yesterday and
                    reiterated after Cabinet meeting to-day to do as little <pb facs="0976" n="860"
                        xml:id="pg860"/> damage as possible to the city of Vera Cruz and especially
                    to foreign interests. There is no intention of bombarding the city; fighting
                    will take place outside of city, fire being directed at barracks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
